# Keep the build context small and keep local state out of image layers.
#
# An image layer is readable by anyone who can pull it, so a stray .env or a
# local database baked into a layer is a leak that survives deleting the file
# in a later commit (RULE-2).

.git
.github
.githooks

# Local working state — never source, and never in an image.
#
# Patterns here are filepath.Match-style, NOT gitignore-style: `*` does not
# cross a `/`, and a bare pattern is matched against the whole path rather than
# applied at every directory level. So `*.db` alone excludes a database at the
# repo root and silently keeps `.devrun/aff.db` — which is the exact file this
# section exists to keep out. Every pattern that must match at any depth is
# written `**/`.
.env
.env.*
**/*.key
recovery-codes*
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/backups/

# The local dev run directory: AFF_SECRET_KEY, the dev admin password and TOTP
# secret, and a live database (see .devrun/env.sh). It never reaches the
# published image — the runtime stage copies three explicit paths out of the
# build stage and this is not one of them — but without this line it is
# uploaded in the build context and baked into a build-stage layer, which is
# exported by registry-backed build caches (RULE-2).
.devrun/

# Build output; the image builds its own.
bin/
dist/
web/dist/
*.exe

# Docs do not affect the binary, and excluding them means a typo fix does not
# invalidate the build cache.
*.md
docs/
design/

# Test artefacts
coverage/
cover.out
*.out
